Han reference provenance

Reference versions, source URLs and archive checksums are recorded in the
provenance headers. Per-value records distinguish blind predictions, independent
reading agreement and transcription from one lineage. Those labels do not
establish a public-domain status or a distribution license. A release license
verdict depends on the assembled corpus and its retained provenance.
Prediction logs identify decomposition sources by id and pinned revision and
record only input checksums. Verbatim decomposition inputs, prompts and raw
responses require their own source-license determination before distribution;
blind prediction, source pointers and checksums do not confer those rights.

